    {
      "id": "f1g7xmk",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. List of Fundamental Rights"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Fundamental Rights are covered under Part III of the Indian Constitution, spanning Articles 12 through 35.",
        "Articles 12 and 13 define the 'State' and establish laws inconsistent with or in derogation of Fundamental Rights as void.",
        "Right to Equality (Articles 14–18) provides for equality before law, prohibition of discrimination, equality of opportunity, and abolition of untouchability and titles.",
        "Right to Freedom (Articles 19–22) guarantees six fundamental freedoms, subject to reasonable restrictions defined under the Constitution.",
        "Article 32 provides Constitutional Remedies, authorizing the Supreme Court to issue writs for the enforcement of Fundamental Rights."
      ],
      "id": "0crx8ol"
    },
