      "content": "8. Right to Constitutional Remedies (Articles 32–35)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nqb0gja",
      "content": "Citizens can approach Supreme Court or High Court to enforce Fundamental Rights."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Dr. B.R. Ambedkar referred to Article 32 (Right to Constitutional Remedies) as the 'Heart and Soul' of the Constitution.",
        "The five types of writs under Article 32 are Habeas Corpus, Mandamus, Prohibition, Certiorari, and Quo-Warranto.",
        "Right to Property was deleted from the list of Fundamental Rights by the 44th Constitutional Amendment Act, 1978."
      ],
      "id": "tantk2b"
    },
    {
      "id": "no5z3y3",
